<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sierra Leone Company</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1791–1808</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sierra-leone">Sierra Leone</a> Company was a British chartered company founded in 1791 by abolitionists to run a settlement for freed Black people on the Sierra Leone peninsula. It took over the failed Province of Freedom, founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/freetown">Freetown</a> in 1792 with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-loyalists">Black Loyalists</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nova-scotia">Nova Scotia</a>, and handed the colony to the Crown in 1808.</p></div>
